Windows Fundamentals Part 1

Overview

This room introduces the Windows operating system, its interface, and basic system administration tools.

Topics Learned

* Windows desktop and user interface
* File system and folders
* System configuration
* Task Manager
* System Information

Tools and Features

Task Manager

Used to view running applications, processes, and system resource usage.

File Explorer

Used to browse files, folders, and storage devices.

System Information

Displays information about the computer’s hardware and software configuration.

Settings and Control Panel

Used to configure Windows system settings.

Cybersecurity Relevance

Understanding Windows helps security analysts investigate running processes, inspect system configuration, and troubleshoot suspicious activity.

